.TH KERB.PY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
kerb.py \- print the default Kerberos principal, the default realm and every cached principal (deprecated)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 kerb.py
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Deprecated.
Superseded by
.BR krb\-caches (1)
.RB ( "krb\-caches \-\-json" )
and
.B mu2edaq\-krb list
from
.BR mu2edaq\-kerberos ,
which also report the cache names and backend.
.PP
Prints, one per line: the principal of the default cache
(python\-krb5 object repr, e.g.
.BR b'mu2edaq/mu2edaq/mu2e.fnal.gov@FNAL.GOV' ),
the default realm, then the principal of every cache in the collection
that has one.
.PP
It imports
.B gssapi
without using it;
.B gssapi
is not in
.IR requirements.txt ,
so in a venv made by
.B bootstrap.sh
the script fails at import.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B KRB5CCNAME
selects the default cache and collection.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0; 1 with a traceback when an import fails or the default cache is empty
or missing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
venv/bin/pip install gssapi && venv/bin/python kerb.py
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR krb\-caches (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-krb (1),
.BR klist (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
